{"toolCallId":"call_9755a24fb248425391029985b698c135","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nSet these two variables before running any `Verify:` command:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the pre-change stdout of three invocations into `$P/scratch/baseline/` (`$S`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n- [ ] T002 Read the argument loop, `output_text`, `output_json` and the output dispatch, and note the three insertion points (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm no caller passes `--quiet` today (`.skilled/commands`, `.skilled/skills`). Verify: `grep -rn 'recommend-level\\.sh.*--quiet' .skilled/commands .skilled/skills --include=*.yaml --include=*.sh --include=*.json | wc -l` prints 0.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Confirm the current script is lint-clean (`$S`). Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^QUIET_OUTPUT=false$' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet)` arm to the argument loop (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints only the `Recommended Level:` line (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^output_quiet()' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T008 Dispatch JSON first, then quiet, then text (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` and its `--json` precedence in `show_help` and the header OPTIONS block (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Compare the quiet line with the default report's level line (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | grep '^Recommended Level:') <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Re-capture the three default invocations into `$P/scratch/after/` and diff them against the baseline (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff -r \"$P\"/scratch/baseline \"$P\"/scratch/after` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T012 Verify `--json` precedence in both flag orders (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] T013 Verify error paths keep their exit code and message (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `At least --loc or --files` on stderr.\n- [ ] T014 Run the static checks (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` and `shellcheck \"$S\"` both exit 0.\n- [ ] T015 Clean the scratch outputs and record the observed results in `implementation-summary.md` (`$P`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decisions**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA row marked `N/A` is verified as not applicable and is ticked when that reason is true. A real row is ticked only after its `Verify:` command printed the stated output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^| REQ-' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### Step ' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 4.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies available. Verify: `bash --version | head -1` prints 3.2 or later.\n- [ ] CHK-004 [P1] Pre-change baseline captured. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Syntax check passes. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] Lint check passes. Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error paths unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 with the same stderr text as before the change.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The branch matches the file's shape: one global, one case arm, one output function. Verify: `grep -c 'QUIET_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Quiet output is one line for the three representative invocations. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] `--json` precedence verified in both flag orders. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Repeated and reordered `--quiet` verified. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --quiet --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] N/A: no finding drives this packet, so finding classes and adversarial tables do not apply.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory: every producer of the level label is named. Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1 and the quiet branch reuses that literal.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory: every caller of the script is named. Verify: `grep -rln 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/commands .skilled/skills | wc -l` matches the surface table in `plan.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No secrets added. Verify: `git diff -- \"$S\"` adds no credential, token or key literal.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc abc --files 2` exits 1 with `must be a positive integer`.\n- [x] CHK-032 [P1] N/A: the script has no authentication or authorization surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan, tasks and acceptance criteria agree on `--quiet` and on the `--json` precedence. Verify: `grep -l -- '--quiet' \"$P\"/*.md` lists all four documents.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header and `--help` describe the flag. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-042 [P2] N/A: no README documents this script's individual flags; `--help` is the flag contract.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp outputs live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `git status --porcelain \"$S\" \"$P\"` lists only the script and the packet docs.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 14 | 2/14 |\n| P1 Items | 20 | 6/20 |\n| P2 Items | 8 | 6/8 |\n\nThe two verified P0 rows, the six verified P1 rows and the six verified P2 rows are the `N/A` rows, whose reason is stated inline. Every other row is open because the feature is planned, not implemented.\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is recorded in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### ADR-001:' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] ADR-001 carries a status. Verify: `grep -c '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Accepted' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives carry rejection reasons. Verify: `sed -n '/Alternatives Rejected/,/^---/p' \"$P/plan.md\" | grep -c '^\\- '` prints 2.\n- [x] CHK-103 [P2] N/A: the change is additive, so no migration path exists.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [x] CHK-110 [P1] N/A: the packet makes no performance claim; the flag adds one branch and one line of output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented. Verify: `grep -c 'Revert the single commit' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-121 [P0] N/A: `--quiet` is opt-in per invocation; there is no runtime flag to configure.\n- [x] CHK-122 [P1] N/A: no service is deployed, so there is nothing to monitor.\n- [x] CHK-123 [P1] N/A: no runbook is needed; the script is invoked directly.\n- [x] CHK-124 [P2] N/A: no deployment step exists.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [x] CHK-130 [P1] N/A: no security surface changes; the script reads no credential.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency license change. Verify: `git diff --stat -- \"$S\"` shows one file and no manifest.\n- [x] CHK-132 [P2] N/A: no web surface, so OWASP does not apply.\n- [x] CHK-133 [P2] N/A: the change handles no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Verify: `grep -c -- '--quiet' \"$P\"/spec.md \"$P\"/plan.md \"$P\"/tasks.md \"$P\"/acceptance-criteria.md` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [x] CHK-141 [P1] N/A: the script exposes no API documentation surface.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-143 [P2] N/A: no knowledge transfer is needed beyond this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Operator | Technical Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Pending | |\n| Operator | QA Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nSet these two variables before running any `Verify:` command:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the pre-change stdout of three invocations into `$P/scratch/baseline/` (`$S`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n- [ ] T002 Read the argument loop, `output_text`, `output_json` and the output dispatch, and note the three insertion points (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm no caller passes `--quiet` today (`.skilled/commands`, `.skilled/skills`). Verify: `grep -rn 'recommend-level\\.sh.*--quiet' .skilled/commands .skilled/skills --include=*.yaml --include=*.sh --include=*.json | wc -l` prints 0.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Confirm the current script is lint-clean (`$S`). Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^QUIET_OUTPUT=false$' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet)` arm to the argument loop (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints only the `Recommended Level:` line (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^output_quiet()' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T008 Dispatch JSON first, then quiet, then text (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` and its `--json` precedence in `show_help` and the header OPTIONS block (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Compare the quiet line with the default report's level line (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | grep '^Recommended Level:') <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Re-capture the three default invocations into `$P/scratch/after/` and diff them against the baseline (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff -r \"$P\"/scratch/baseline \"$P\"/scratch/after` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T012 Verify `--json` precedence in both flag orders (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] T013 Verify error paths keep their exit code and message (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `At least --loc or --files` on stderr.\n- [ ] T014 Run the static checks (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` and `shellcheck \"$S\"` both exit 0.\n- [ ] T015 Clean the scratch outputs and record the observed results in `implementation-summary.md` (`$P`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decisions**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA row marked `N/A` is verified as not applicable and is ticked when that reason is true. A real row is ticked only after its `Verify:` command printed the stated output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^| REQ-' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### Step ' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 4.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies available. Verify: `bash --version | head -1` prints 3.2 or later.\n- [ ] CHK-004 [P1] Pre-change baseline captured. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Syntax check passes. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] Lint check passes. Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error paths unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 with the same stderr text as before the change.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The branch matches the file's shape: one global, one case arm, one output function. Verify: `grep -c 'QUIET_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Quiet output is one line for the three representative invocations. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] `--json` precedence verified in both flag orders. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Repeated and reordered `--quiet` verified. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --quiet --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] N/A: no finding drives this packet, so finding classes and adversarial tables do not apply.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory: every producer of the level label is named. Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1 and the quiet branch reuses that literal.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory: every caller of the script is named. Verify: `grep -rln 'recommend-level\\.sh' .skilled/commands | wc -l` prints 3, and all three files appear in the surface table in `plan.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No secrets added. Verify: `git diff -- \"$S\"` adds no credential, token or key literal.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc abc --files 2` exits 1 with `must be a positive integer`.\n- [x] CHK-032 [P1] N/A: the script has no authentication or authorization surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan, tasks and acceptance criteria agree on `--quiet` and on the `--json` precedence. Verify: `grep -l -- '--quiet' \"$P\"/*.md` lists all four documents.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header and `--help` describe the flag. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-042 [P2] N/A: no README documents this script's individual flags; `--help` is the flag contract.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp outputs live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `git status --porcelain \"$S\" \"$P\"` lists only the script and the packet docs.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 14 | 2/14 |\n| P1 Items | 20 | 6/20 |\n| P2 Items | 8 | 6/8 |\n\nThe two verified P0 rows, the six verified P1 rows and the six verified P2 rows are the `N/A` rows, whose reason is stated inline. Every other row is open because the feature is planned, not implemented.\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is recorded in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### ADR-001:' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] ADR-001 carries a status. Verify: `grep -c '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Accepted' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives carry rejection reasons. Verify: `sed -n '/Alternatives Rejected/,/^---/p' \"$P/plan.md\" | grep -c '^\\- '` prints 2.\n- [x] CHK-103 [P2] N/A: the change is additive, so no migration path exists.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [x] CHK-110 [P1] N/A: the packet makes no performance claim; the flag adds one branch and one line of output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented. Verify: `grep -c 'Revert the single commit' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-121 [P0] N/A: `--quiet` is opt-in per invocation; there is no runtime flag to configure.\n- [x] CHK-122 [P1] N/A: no service is deployed, so there is nothing to monitor.\n- [x] CHK-123 [P1] N/A: no runbook is needed; the script is invoked directly.\n- [x] CHK-124 [P2] N/A: no deployment step exists.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [x] CHK-130 [P1] N/A: no security surface changes; the script reads no credential.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] No dependency license change. Verify: `git diff --stat -- \"$S\"` shows one file and no manifest.\n- [x] CHK-132 [P2] N/A: no web surface, so OWASP does not apply.\n- [x] CHK-133 [P2] N/A: the change handles no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents are synchronized. Verify: `grep -c -- '--quiet' \"$P\"/spec.md \"$P\"/plan.md \"$P\"/tasks.md \"$P\"/acceptance-criteria.md` prints a non-zero count for each file.\n- [x] CHK-141 [P1] N/A: the script exposes no API documentation surface.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-143 [P2] N/A: no knowledge transfer is needed beyond this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Operator | Technical Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Pending | |\n| Operator | QA Lead | [ ] Pending | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_9addca5416d244309c3d697ae4e3b966","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh prints a multi-line report whose first line carries the recommended level, so a caller that needs only that value must filter the report or parse JSON. This packet specifies a --quiet flag that prints the level line alone and leaves every existing invocation unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level one line output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` answers one question, the recommended SpecKit level, but it prints a multi-line report to do it: a score and confidence line, a five-row breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A caller that wants only the answer either filters that report or runs `--json` and parses a document, and the filter route makes the label and line order an undocumented contract that each caller re-implements. This packet adds a `--quiet` flag that prints the single `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` line, with the default text output and the `--json` document left byte-identical.\n\n**Key Decisions**: A boolean `--quiet` flag selects the one-line text output (ADR-001); `--json` keeps precedence when both flags are passed.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: bash 3.2+ and coreutils, both already required by the script. No new package.\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe script answers one question, the recommended level, but prints a multi-line report to do it. A caller that needs only that value pipes the report through `grep` or `head`, or runs `--json` and parses a document; the `grep` route repeats the label in every caller and turns line order into a contract nobody wrote down.\n\n### Purpose\nA caller can read the recommended level as one line with no parsing, while every existing invocation keeps exactly the output it prints today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` and exits 0.\n- Keep the default text output and the `--json` document byte-identical.\n- Document the flag in `--help` and in the script header's OPTIONS block.\n- Define and test the precedence when `--quiet` and `--json` are both passed.\n- Record the pre-change output as a baseline so the default path can be diffed.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Scoring, thresholds, phase logic and confidence math - the flag changes output selection only.\n- A `-q` short form, an environment variable or a config file - one caller needs the long form today, and each extra switch is another permanent branch.\n- Migrating `speckit-plan.yaml` or `speckit-complete.yaml` to `--quiet` - both callers want the JSON document.\n- A new automated test harness for the script - the repository has none for this file, and shell assertions prove the contract.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the flag, one output function, one dispatch branch and the help text |\n| `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/*.md` | Modify | This specification, the plan, the tasks and the acceptance criteria |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted on any valid invocation and stdout is exactly one line, `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`, with exit status 0. |\n| REQ-002 | Without `--quiet`, stdout and stderr are byte-identical to the pre-change script for the same arguments, including the `--json` and `--no-recommend-phases` paths. |\n| REQ-003 | `--quiet` changes no error path: invalid input still writes its existing message to stderr and exits 1, and a successful quiet run writes nothing to stderr. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--help` lists `--quiet` in its OPTIONS block and the script header documents it beside the other flags. |\n| REQ-005 | When `--quiet` and `--json` are both passed, the JSON document is printed unchanged and no text line is added. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- **SC-002**: The quiet line equals the `Recommended Level:` line of the default report for the same arguments; `diff` prints nothing.\n- **SC-003**: The default output for three representative invocations diffs clean against the baseline captured before the edit.\n- **SC-004**: `bash -n` and `shellcheck` exit 0, and `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | bash 3.2+ and coreutils (`wc`, `diff`) | The script cannot run | Already required today; the change adds no dependency |\n| Dependency | `shellcheck` for the lint gate | The lint check is skipped | `bash -n` still gates syntax; record the skip if `shellcheck` is absent |\n| Risk | A caller parses the quiet line and a later label change breaks it | Med | SC-002 pins the line to the label the default report already prints; the label is not new |\n| Risk | Adding a branch drifts the default output | High | Capture the baseline before the edit (T001) and diff after (T011) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: N/A. The change adds one branch and one line of output; it has no timing or throughput target and makes no performance claim.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: N/A. The script reads no credential, writes no file and reaches no network; input validation is unchanged.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: No new failure mode. Every error path keeps its current exit code and message, and `set -euo pipefail` stays in force.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: no `--loc` and no `--files` still exits 1 with `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided`, with or without `--quiet`.\n- Maximum values: `--loc 1000` and `--files 30` still print one line, with the Level 3 label.\n- Zero on one axis: `--loc 0 --files 2` is valid today and prints one quiet line.\n- Boundary score: a total within 5 points of a level boundary still prints one line; only confidence changes, and confidence is not printed.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- Unknown option: `ERROR: Unknown option: <flag>` on stderr, exit 1; `--quiet` does not suppress it.\n- Missing value: `--loc` followed by another flag keeps `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value`, exit 1.\n- Non-numeric value: `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`, exit 1.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Repeated `--quiet`: the flag is idempotent.\n- Flag order: `--quiet` before, between or after other flags produces the same one-line output.\n- JSON precedence: `--json --quiet` and `--quiet --json` both print the JSON document.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 8/25 | Files: 1 script, LOC: ~20 net, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 10/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (stdout is a shared caller contract) |\n| Research | 8/20 | Caller inventory across `.skilled/commands` and `.skilled/skills` |\n| Multi-Agent | 2/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 6/15 | Script, help text and four packet docs must agree on one flag name and one label |\n| **Total** | **34/100** | **Content scores Level 1; authored at Level 3 so a shared output contract gets the full specification and regression proof** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | A caller parses the quiet line and a later label change breaks it | M | L | SC-002 ties the quiet line to the label the default report already prints |\n| R-002 | A later edit reorders the dispatch and `--json` loses precedence | M | L | AC-007 tests both flag orders; ADR-001 records the precedence |\n| R-003 | The default output drifts while the branch is added | H | L | Baseline captured before the edit (T001) and diffed after (T011) |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: Read the level as one line (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** build or release script, **I want** the recommended level on one line, **so that** I can read it with `$(...)` without parsing the full report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Keep the full report by default (Priority: P1)\n\n**As an** operator running the script by hand, **I want** the full report when I pass no flag, **so that** I keep the score, breakdown and phase recommendation I read today.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Should `--quiet` suppress the phase recommendation fields? RESOLVED: Yes. Quiet mode prints only the level line, and phase scoring still runs for `--json`.\n- Should `--quiet` and `--json` be mutually exclusive? RESOLVED: No. `--json` wins, so an existing JSON caller that adds `--quiet` still gets its document (ADR-001).\n- Should `--quiet` have a `-q` short form? RESOLVED: No. The request names the long form, and a second spelling is a second branch to document and test.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001)\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"recommend-level.sh prints a multi-line report whose first line carries the recommended level, so a caller that needs only that value must filter the report or parse JSON. This packet specifies a --quiet flag that prints the level line alone and leaves every existing invocation unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level one line output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` answers one question, the recommended SpecKit level, but it prints a multi-line report to do it: a score and confidence line, a five-row breakdown and a phase-recommendation block. A caller that wants only the answer either filters that report or runs `--json` and parses a document, and the filter route makes the label and line order an undocumented contract that each caller re-implements. This packet adds a `--quiet` flag that prints the single `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` line, with the default text output and the `--json` document left byte-identical.\n\n**Key Decisions**: A boolean `--quiet` flag selects the one-line text output (ADR-001); `--json` keeps precedence when both flags are passed.\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: bash 3.2+ and coreutils, both already required by the script. No new package.\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`recommend-level.sh` prints a multi-line report when a caller needs only the recommended level. That caller pipes the report through `grep` or `head`, or runs `--json` and parses a document; the `grep` route repeats the label in every caller and turns line order into a contract nobody wrote down.\n\n### Purpose\nA caller can read the recommended level as one line with no parsing, while every existing invocation keeps exactly the output it prints today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)` and exits 0.\n- Keep the default text output and the `--json` document byte-identical.\n- Document the flag in `--help` and in the script header's OPTIONS block.\n- Define and test the precedence when `--quiet` and `--json` are both passed.\n- Record the pre-change output as a baseline so the default path can be diffed.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Scoring, thresholds, phase logic and confidence math - the flag changes output selection only.\n- A `-q` short form, an environment variable or a config file - one caller needs the long form today, and each extra switch is another permanent branch.\n- Migrating `speckit-plan.yaml` or `speckit-complete.yaml` to `--quiet` - both callers want the JSON document.\n- A new automated test harness for the script - the repository has none for this file, and shell assertions prove the contract.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add the flag, one output function, one dispatch branch and the help text |\n| `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/*.md` | Modify | This specification, the plan, the tasks and the acceptance criteria |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted on any valid invocation and stdout is exactly one line, `Recommended Level: <N> (<Name>)`, with exit status 0. |\n| REQ-002 | Without `--quiet`, stdout and stderr are byte-identical to the pre-change script for the same arguments, including the `--json` and `--no-recommend-phases` paths. |\n| REQ-003 | `--quiet` changes no error path: invalid input still writes its existing message to stderr and exits 1, and a successful quiet run writes nothing to stderr. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--help` lists `--quiet` in its OPTIONS block and the script header documents it beside the other flags. |\n| REQ-005 | When `--quiet` and `--json` are both passed, the JSON document is printed unchanged and no text line is added. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `bash recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet | wc -l` prints `1`.\n- **SC-002**: The quiet line equals the `Recommended Level:` line of the default report for the same arguments; `diff` prints nothing.\n- **SC-003**: The default output for three representative invocations diffs clean against the baseline captured before the edit.\n- **SC-004**: `bash -n` and `shellcheck` exit 0, and `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | bash 3.2+ and coreutils (`wc`, `diff`) | The script cannot run | Already required today; the change adds no dependency |\n| Dependency | `shellcheck` for the lint gate | The lint check is skipped | `bash -n` still gates syntax; record the skip if `shellcheck` is absent |\n| Risk | A caller parses the quiet line and a later label change breaks it | Med | SC-002 pins the line to the label the default report already prints; the label is not new |\n| Risk | Adding a branch drifts the default output | High | Capture the baseline before the edit (T001) and diff after (T011) |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: N/A. The change adds one branch and one line of output; it has no timing or throughput target and makes no performance claim.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: N/A. The script reads no credential, writes no file and reaches no network; input validation is unchanged.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: No new failure mode. Every error path keeps its current exit code and message, and `set -euo pipefail` stays in force.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: no `--loc` and no `--files` still exits 1 with `ERROR: At least --loc or --files must be provided`, with or without `--quiet`.\n- Maximum values: `--loc 1000` and `--files 30` still print one line, with the Level 3 label.\n- Zero on one axis: `--loc 0 --files 2` is valid today and prints one quiet line.\n- Boundary score: a total within 5 points of a level boundary still prints one line; only confidence changes, and confidence is not printed.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- Unknown option: `ERROR: Unknown option: <flag>` on stderr, exit 1; `--quiet` does not suppress it.\n- Missing value: `--loc` followed by another flag keeps `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value`, exit 1.\n- Non-numeric value: `ERROR: --loc must be a positive integer`, exit 1.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Repeated `--quiet`: the flag is idempotent.\n- Flag order: `--quiet` before, between or after other flags produces the same one-line output.\n- JSON precedence: `--json --quiet` and `--quiet --json` both print the JSON document.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 8/25 | Files: 1 script, LOC: ~20 net, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 10/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N (stdout is a shared caller contract) |\n| Research | 8/20 | Caller inventory across `.skilled/commands` and `.skilled/skills` |\n| Multi-Agent | 2/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 6/15 | Script, help text and four packet docs must agree on one flag name and one label |\n| **Total** | **34/100** | **Content scores Level 1; authored at Level 3 so a shared output contract gets the full specification and regression proof** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | A caller parses the quiet line and a later label change breaks it | M | L | SC-002 ties the quiet line to the label the default report already prints |\n| R-002 | A later edit reorders the dispatch and `--json` loses precedence | M | L | AC-007 tests both flag orders; ADR-001 records the precedence |\n| R-003 | The default output drifts while the branch is added | H | L | Baseline captured before the edit (T001) and diffed after (T011) |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: Read the level as one line (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** build or release script, **I want** the recommended level on one line, **so that** I can read it with `$(...)` without parsing the full report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: Keep the full report by default (Priority: P1)\n\n**As an** operator running the script by hand, **I want** the full report when I pass no flag, **so that** I keep the score, breakdown and phase recommendation I read today.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Should `--quiet` suppress the phase recommendation fields? RESOLVED: Yes. Quiet mode prints only the level line, and phase scoring still runs for `--json`.\n- Should `--quiet` and `--json` be mutually exclusive? RESOLVED: No. `--json` wins, so an existing JSON caller that adds `--quiet` still gets its document (ADR-001).\n- Should `--quiet` have a `-q` short form? RESOLVED: No. The request names the long form, and a second spelling is a second branch to document and test.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001)\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
