{"toolCallId":"call_d88aaf7b116a43d8942b00e25387ce2b","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w27ef8e22cd/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure (`<folder>`). Verify: `ls <folder>` lists it.\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies (`<manifest>`). Verify: `<install command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools (`<config>`). Verify: `<tool> --version` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually (`<file>`). Verify: `<command>` prints <expected output>.\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases (`<test>`). Verify: `<test command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation (`<doc>`). Verify: `rg -n '<term>' <doc>` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Fill each checklist section below. GOOD: Each CHK line names the command that answers it. WEAK: The checklist is done. -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three rows and add the rule this packet uses for a blocked task. GOOD: P0 blocks close. P1 needs a recorded reason. WEAK: Follow the priorities. -->\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per setup fact, each with a command. GOOD: CHK-001 [P0] The start commit is in `goal.md` section 4. WEAK: Setup is ready. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file rule. A command must answer it. GOOD: CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n recommend-level.sh` exits 0. WEAK: Code is clean. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Code passes lint/format checks\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No console errors or warnings\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error handling implemented\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] Code follows project patterns\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per acceptance criterion. GOOD: CHK-020 [P0] `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: Tests pass. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual testing complete\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n<!-- FILL: Keep this section, because every level requires it. Write one check per finding class this packet can produce. Delete only the rows that do not apply, never the section. GOOD: CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Every finding names one class. WEAK: All findings handled. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed, or instance-only status proven by grep.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed for changed helpers, policies, schema fields, response fields, docs, and tests.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Security/path/parser/redaction fixes include adversarial table tests for delimiter, joined-input, outside-root, no-op, and fallback cases.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count are listed before completion is claimed.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile env/global-state variant executed when tests or code read process-wide state.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a fix SHA or explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per security surface. Write `N/A` with a reason when none applies. GOOD: CHK-030 [P0] The script reads no credential. WEAK: Security is fine. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation implemented\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz working correctly\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per document that must agree. GOOD: CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md` and `tasks.md` name the same flag. WEAK: Docs are updated. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec/plan/tasks synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] Code comments adequate\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README updated (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n<!-- FILL: Write one check per file location rule. GOOD: CHK-050 [P1] Test copies live under `scratch/test/`. WEAK: Files are organized. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp files in scratch/ only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] scratch/ cleaned before completion\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n<!-- FILL: Count the boxes by priority and write the three totals. GOOD: P0 12, P1 13, P2 1. WEAK: Most items done. -->\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | [X] | [ ]/[X] |\n| P1 Items | [Y] | [ ]/[Y] |\n| P2 Items | [Z] | [ ]/[Z] |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per ADR, or delete the section when the packet records no ADR. GOOD: CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T002. WEAK: Architecture is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] Architecture decisions documented in decision-record.md\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have status (Proposed/Accepted)\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path documented (if applicable)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per performance claim, or delete the section when the packet makes none. GOOD: CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds under 5 ms. WEAK: Performance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] Response time targets met (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] Throughput targets met (NFR-P02)\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing completed\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Performance benchmarks documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per deployment step, or delete the section when the packet ships no service. GOOD: CHK-120 [P0] The rollback command was run in a copy. WEAK: Ready to deploy. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] Feature flag configured (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] Monitoring/alerting configured\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] Runbook created\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook reviewed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per compliance surface, or delete the section when none applies. GOOD: CHK-130 [P1] No license changed. WEAK: Compliance is verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review completed\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses compatible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\n  - \"quiet flag implementation tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nSet these two variables before running any `Verify:` command:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the pre-change stdout of three invocations into `$P/scratch/baseline/` (`$S`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n- [ ] T002 Read the argument loop, `output_text`, `output_json` and the output dispatch, and note the three insertion points (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm no caller passes `--quiet` today (`.skilled/commands`, `.skilled/skills`). Verify: `grep -rn -- '--quiet' .skilled/commands .skilled/skills | grep -c 'recommend-level'` prints 0.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Confirm the current script is lint-clean (`$S`). Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T005 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` beside `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^QUIET_OUTPUT=false$' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--quiet)` arm to the argument loop (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2` exits 0.\n- [ ] T007 Add `output_quiet()` that prints only the `Recommended Level:` line (`$S`). Verify: `grep -c '^output_quiet()' \"$S\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] T008 Dispatch JSON first, then quiet, then text (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` and its `--json` precedence in `show_help` and the header OPTIONS block (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T010 Compare the quiet line with the default report's level line (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural | grep '^Recommended Level:') <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Re-capture the three default invocations into `$P/scratch/after/` and diff them against the baseline (`$P/scratch/`). Verify: `diff -r \"$P\"/scratch/baseline \"$P\"/scratch/after` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T012 Verify `--json` precedence in both flag orders (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --json --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] T013 Verify error paths keep their exit code and message (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 and prints `At least --loc or --files` on stderr.\n- [ ] T014 Run the static checks (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` and `shellcheck \"$S\"` both exit 0.\n- [ ] T015 Clean the scratch outputs and record the observed results in `implementation-summary.md` (`$P`). Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `validate.sh --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decisions**: See `plan.md` (ADR-001)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n\nA row marked `N/A` is verified as not applicable and is ticked when that reason is true. A real row is ticked only after its `Verify:` command printed the stated output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in `spec.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^| REQ-' \"$P/spec.md\"` prints 5.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### Step ' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 4.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies available. Verify: `bash --version | head -1` prints 3.2 or later.\n- [ ] CHK-004 [P1] Pre-change baseline captured. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch/baseline | wc -l` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] Syntax check passes. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] Lint check passes. Verify: `shellcheck \"$S\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Error paths unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` exits 1 with the same stderr text as before the change.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The branch matches the file's shape: one global, one case arm, one output function. Verify: `grep -c 'QUIET_OUTPUT' \"$S\"` prints 3.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` is `Met`.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Quiet output is one line for the three representative invocations. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | wc -l` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] `--json` precedence verified in both flag orders. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --quiet --loc 50 --files 2 | jq -e .recommended_level` prints a number.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Repeated and reordered `--quiet` verified. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 50 --quiet --files 2 --quiet | wc -l` prints 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] N/A: no finding drives this packet, so finding classes and adversarial tables do not apply.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory: every producer of the level label is named. Verify: `grep -c 'Recommended Level:' \"$S\"` prints 1 and the quiet branch reuses that literal.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory: every caller of the script is named. Verify: `grep -rln 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/commands .skilled/skills | wc -l` matches the surface table in `plan.md`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No secrets added. Verify: `git diff -- \"$S\"` adds no credential, token or key literal.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --quiet --loc abc --files 2` exits 1 with `must be a positive integer`.\n- [x] CHK-032 [P1] N/A: the script has no authentication or authorization surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan, tasks and acceptance criteria agree on `--quiet` and on the `--json` precedence. Verify: `grep -l -- '--quiet' \"$P\"/*.md` lists all four documents.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The script header and `--help` describe the flag. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | grep -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-042 [P2] N/A: no README documents this script's individual flags; `--help` is the flag contract.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Temp outputs live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `git status --porcelain \"$S\" \"$P\"` lists only the script and the packet docs.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` cleaned before completion. Verify: `ls \"$P\"/scratch` lists only `.gitkeep`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 14 | 0/14 |\n| P1 Items | 20 | 2/20 |\n| P2 Items | 8 | 6/8 |\n\nThe two verified P1 rows and the six verified P2 rows are the `N/A` rows, whose reason is stated inline. Every other row is open because the feature is planned, not implemented.\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is recorded in `plan.md`. Verify: `grep -c '^### ADR-001:' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] ADR-001 carries a status. Verify: `grep -c '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*: Accepted' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives carry rejection reasons. Verify: `sed -n '/Alternatives Rejected/,/^---/p' \"$P/plan.md\" | grep -c '^\\- '` prints 2.\n- [x] CHK-103 [P2] N/A: the change is additive, so no migration path exists.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [x] CHK-110 [P1] N/A: the packet makes no performance claim; the flag adds one branch and one line of output.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented. Verify: `grep -c 'Revert the single commit' \"$P/plan.md\"` prints 1.\n- [x] CHK-121 [P0] N/A: `--quiet` is opt-in per invocation; there is no runtime flag to configure.\n- [x] CHK-122 [P1] N/A: no service is deployed, so there is nothing to monitor.\n- [x] CHK-123 [P1] N/A: no runbook is needed; the script is invoked directly.\n- [x] CHK-124 [P2] N/A: no deployment step exist